{
  "comment": "Why: the Nine Hells as an industry have a workforce, not a wilderness: imps on every errand (vex and blaze), the damned who work the lines (wither skeletons), hounds of the yard (Tensura's barghest), slag that crawls out of the troughs (magma cubes), overseers in black iron (living armour and piglin brutes), and the demon tag itself, which is the crew of the shift. The table never uses the dark (a foundry is lit by what it burns) and nothing in it is a wilderness animal: every entry is somebody's job, and the hard ones are supervisors. The roll bonus is plus one and the budget scale 1.3: the Hells are not bigger than the Abyss, but they are better organised. Two entries use the Blood War on purpose: the demon tag against the undead tag, which are rivals in the faction files.",
